# Each testdata/v1/*.ergo is a byte-for-byte copy of the check-v1 acceptance
# rule of the same name. Source: the orchestrator-owned acceptance tree,
# /home/exedev/.cache/baton/wf10/check-v1/accept/rules/<name> (copied as each
# stage lands; last synced at stage E4 round 1). TestV1Manifest requires each
# copy to have its line here, with this hash. Detect drift from the source:
#   cd /home/exedev/.cache/baton/wf10/check-v1/accept/rules && sha256sum -c <this file>
# 196w: the D7-satisfaction copies spell the construct keyword context; the
# source rules take the same rename when the orchestrator syncs them.
# 196n: C4-rows.pos spells its capability rows with |; the source rule takes the
# same respelling when the orchestrator syncs it.
# G9 (std-1): the G9-extern-allowlist rules are new; their source is
# /home/exedev/.cache/baton/wf10/g9/accept/<name> until the orchestrator syncs
# them into the acceptance tree.
